---
import R from './R.astro';

const pms = { au: 'Cliniko', uk: 'Dentally or Cliniko' };
const busy = { au: 'HICAPS claims', uk: 'payments' };
---
<section class="border-y border-hairline bg-surface" aria-labelledby="leak-title">
  <div class="container-page section">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 id="leak-title" class="h2 text-ink">Where high-value calls go missing</h2>
      <p class="lede mt-4">
        Implant, Invisalign and veneer enquiries rarely leave a voicemail. They ring the next practice on the map. Three gaps cause most of it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-0">
      <article class="md:border-r md:border-hairline md:pr-10">
        <p class="font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,4.5vw,3.5rem)] leading-none text-ink tnum">12:50–1:50</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink">Lunch and after hours</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate">
          The front desk closes for lunch and again at 5:30, just when people ring after clicking your Google ad. Every unanswered call is a
          patient deciding somewhere else.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="md:border-r md:border-hairline md:px-10">
        <p class="font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,4.5vw,3.5rem)] leading-none text-ink">4 rings</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink">A busy front desk</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate">
          Check-ins, <R v={busy} /> and chairside cover all land at once. When the lines stack up, the call that would have booked an implant
          consult rings out.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="md:pl-10">
        <p class="font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,4.5vw,3.5rem)] leading-none text-ink">No re-typing</p>
        <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink">Messages nobody actions</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate">
          Call centres email notes that sit unread until the patient has moved on. Bookings should land in <R v={pms} />, with the notes
          attached.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
